    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 2 tests, 0 failures \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is a derived response field on the owner. I implemented it in two places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `membershipTier` field (and setter used by the mapper).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression to `toOwnerDto`, following the existing `displayName`/`initials` pattern:\n   ```java\n   SILVER when owner.namesakeCount == 0 && email is present, otherwise BRONZE\n   ```\n\nBoth `namesakeCount` (set by `AssignNamesakeCount` at create time) and `email` are existing `Owner` entity fields, so no pipeline/YAML changes were needed \u2014 the tier is computed at serialization time and returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` via the existing `RespondWithOwner` step.\n\nTests: `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique + email \u2192 SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 BRONZE) both pass.",
